# x-release-please-start-version
SET target = "0.0.1"
# x-release-please-end

SET temp = NULL

SET created_paths = []

SET gh_source = "https://github.com/cli/cli/releases"

SET acli_source = "https://developer.atlassian.com/cloud/acli/guides/download-supported-packages/"

DO Detect OS/CPU; resolve private absolute tools under <storage>/tools/bin (.exe on Windows),
    default <user-home>/.inux, honoring overrides and rejecting PATH-only tools. Select
    checksum_verifier: macOS shasum -a 256 -c, Linux sha256sum -c, native Windows equivalent. Use
    short native commands/extraction; no generated installers/helpers/parsers.

DO Create private bin/missing parents one at a time; append each newly created directory to
    created_paths immediately, including partial success. Never track pre-existing directories.
    No package managers/sudo/external symlinks/source builds/PATH/profile edits/compiler/Node
    dependency. In zsh avoid path and keep heredoc terminators alone.

DO Batch availability/version/auth probes, skipping missing tools and capturing every exit as data:
    ix --version (must equal ix <target>), gh --version, gh auth status --hostname github.com, acli
    --version, acli jira auth status.

DO Record inux/github/atlassian: ready = version passed with no requested upgrade; authenticated =
    auth passed. Record setup with complete TRUE only when all versions/both auth checks pass
    without upgrades.

IF setup is complete:
    DO Report probe results.

    STOP "Setup already complete."

DO Set temp to a unique unused absolute path under <storage>/tmp before creating it for all
    metadata/assets/downloads. Create missing parents one at a time, immediately appending each
    newly created parent to created_paths; never track pre-existing directories. Use separate
    installer subdirectories inside temp.

ASYNC github_setup:
    IF github is not ready:
        DO Select the requested gh version or official host release from gh_source.

        CHECK gh archive and exact checksum entry match host OS/CPU.

        DO Download vendor gh archive, verify exact-asset SHA-256 with checksum_verifier, extract,
            and install directly at private gh. Gate each operation on success; preserve working
            tools and set Unix executable permissions where applicable.

        DO Verify private gh --version; inspect only exact help for syntax/version errors.

        DO Probe private gh auth status --hostname github.com; record unauthenticated as data.

    DO Record final gh path, version, and Boolean authenticated field as tool; reuse probes if
        unchanged.

ASYNC atlassian_setup:
    IF atlassian is not ready:
        DO Inspect acli_source once; select supported host standalone binary, honoring upgrades.

        CHECK The host binary is supported and available.

        DO Download official acli binary; verify linked exact-asset checksum with checksum_verifier,
            or report absence and use official HTTPS binary. Stop on mismatch.

        DO Install acli directly at its private path, preserving working tools and Unix executable
            permissions; verify --version. Gate copy on success; inspect help only for
            syntax/version errors.

        DO Probe private acli jira auth status; record unauthenticated as data.

    DO Record final acli path, version, and Boolean authenticated field as tool; reuse probes if
        unchanged.

WAIT github_setup

SET github_result = result of github_setup

SET github = tool of github_result

IF github is not authenticated:
    DO Run private gh auth login --hostname github.com --web; await browser login, keeping
        gh-managed credentials without chat tokens.

    DO Recheck only private gh auth status --hostname github.com; record the result.

IF inux is not ready:
    DO Select repo override or vinod-rightmo/inux, v<target>, and host asset: ix-darwin-amd64,
        ix-darwin-arm64, ix-linux-amd64, ix-linux-arm64, or ix-windows-amd64.exe.

    CHECK The exact target release and host asset exist.

    DO Download ASSET and checksums.txt into temp using private gh release download TAG --repo
        OWNER/REPO --pattern ASSET --pattern checksums.txt --dir TEMP_DIRECTORY with resolved
        literal arguments.

    DO Verify exact ix asset SHA-256 with checksum_verifier, then install directly at private ix
        with Unix executable permissions where applicable. Gate verification/copy on success;
        preserve working tools.

    DO Verify private ix --version equals ix <target> and run --help once; record results.

WAIT atlassian_setup

SET atlassian_result = result of atlassian_setup

SET atlassian = tool of atlassian_result

IF atlassian is not authenticated:
    DO Run private acli jira auth login --web; await browser login, keeping acli-managed credentials
        without chat tokens.

    DO Recheck only private acli jira auth status; record the result.

FINALLY:
    IF temp != NULL:
        DO Remove only this run's temp if it exists; report leftovers/cleanup errors. Preserve
            tools/credentials/task/unrelated files; never repeat successful checks.

    IF created_paths is not empty:
        DO Remove only still-empty directories in created_paths, deepest first; preserve all
            pre-existing/nonempty directories, tools/credentials/task/unrelated files. Report
            leftovers/cleanup errors; never repeat successful checks.

PRINT with compact tool/version/status table, private install directory, failures/checksum/cleanup
    limits; omit successful hashes, metadata, listings, and help output.
